write_pin_placement writes a tcl script, and wrote the pin name bare:

    place_pin -pin_name R0_addr[0] -layer M4 -location {0.042 2.22}

That is not tcl: [0] is a command substitution, and the line only read
back because OpenSTA's global unknown handler turned the unknown command
"0" into a bus subscript.  With that handler scoped to read_sdc
(patches/0003-opensta-read-sdc-scoped-unknown.patch) the script fails
on the first bus pin with invalid command name "0".

Brace the name, so the file the tool writes is the tcl it means:

    place_pin -pin_name {R0_addr[0]} -layer M4 -location {0.042 2.22}

Both emitters, the pin-list one and the bterm one, are changed the same
way.  A braced name reads identically on either interpreter.

Not upstreamed.  Retires on a //:bump onto an OpenROAD carrying it.

diff --git a/src/ppl/src/IOPlacer.cpp b/src/ppl/src/IOPlacer.cpp
index 97a72ca..870b079 100644
--- a/src/ppl/src/IOPlacer.cpp
+++ b/src/ppl/src/IOPlacer.cpp
@@ -722,7 +722,7 @@ void IOPlacer::writePinPlacement(const char* file_name, const bool placed)
           const odb::Rect pin_rect{io_pin.getLowerBound(),
                                    io_pin.getUpperBound()};
           const odb::Point pos = pin_rect.center();
-          out << "place_pin -pin_name " << io_pin.getName() << " -layer "
+          out << "place_pin -pin_name {" << io_pin.getName() << "} -layer "
               << tech_layer->getName() << " -location {"
               << getBlock()->dbuToMicrons(pos.x()) << " "
               << getBlock()->dbuToMicrons(pos.y())
@@ -748,7 +748,7 @@ void IOPlacer::writePinPlacement(const char* file_name, const bool placed)
       }
 
       if (tech_layer != nullptr) {
-        out << "place_pin -pin_name " << bterm->getName() << " -layer "
+        out << "place_pin -pin_name {" << bterm->getName() << "} -layer "
             << tech_layer->getName() << " -location {"
             << getBlock()->dbuToMicrons(x_pos) << " "
             << getBlock()->dbuToMicrons(y_pos) << "}";
